            <ArticleTitle>Obstructive hydrocephalus caused by multiple sclerosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>219-23</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case is reported of obstructive hydrocephalus secondary to the mass effect of a plaque of acute demyelination in the brainstem. The literature on the CT scan appearances in multiple sclerosis is briefly discussed in relation to this case.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
